        "note": [
          {
            "text": "PBS prescription. Previously effective. Rationale documented as moderate–severe postnatal depression and generalized anxiety disorder; breastfeeding compatible, with risks of non-treatment assessed as greater than medication risk."
          },
          {
            "text": "Discussed gastrointestinal side effects, headache, possible initial increased anxiety, onset of effect in 2–4 weeks, and need to continue for 6–12 months once better."
          },
          {
            "text": "Adherence strategies discussed: link dose to morning feed, use phone alarms, and ask mother to remind her."
